 :deliberate-narrowing
 [{:core "cores/resource_scope_core.cljk"
   :rule "path-covers? refuses an empty grant path"
   :why "The host normalizes an absent path to \"/\", so the oracle cannot
         produce \"\" and parity is unaffected. Without it a directly-called
         core would let \"\" cover every absolute path. An assertion in the
         parity test pins that the host never produces one."}]

 :rollback
 {:oracle-retained true
  :method :consumers-already-select-the-oracle
  :data-migration-required false
  :note "Nothing was deleted. Reverting means deleting the .cljk files and
         the parity tests; no call site depends on them."}

 :residual-risk
 ["Parity is over a corpus, not over all strings. Percent-encoded paths and
   non-ASCII hosts are outside it: the oracle's URI.getPath decodes %XX and
   its lower-case is locale-sensitive, and neither is exercised."
  "The capability core compares timestamps lexicographically over code
   points, which equals String.compareTo only for ASCII. ISO-8601 always is,
   and nothing enforces that an :cap/expires string is ISO-8601."
  "Two implementations of each decision now exist. The parity tests are the
   only thing preventing one-sided drift, so a change to either side that
   does not run them can still diverge."
  "This tranche has no soak. q9-migration.edn requires 3 CI runs over 7
   calendar days before promotion, and CI for this repository is the
   murakumo fleet, not GitHub Actions."]

 :promotion
 {:wave-expansion false
